BA_ "Description" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_BrkSwSta "This signal indicates that a brake switch is activated or not. When the brake switch is activated(pressed) its value is 01H otherwise its value is 00H.
If the EMS does not support this signal the value is 02H.

Physical range : 0 ... 100
Conversion : (PH) = (Unsigned)0.002 * (HEX)[%]";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_BrkSwSta 1;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_BrkSwSta 3;
BA_REL_ "GenSigTimeoutTime" BU_SG_REL_ BLTN_CAM SG_ 2214658049 ENG_BrkSwSta 500;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_BrkSwSta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_BrkSwSta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_BrkSwSta "18.11.00";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_ObdFrzFrmSta "An ECU which detects an OBD fault, requires the EMS to store a set of environmental conditions
(freeze frame). If the EMS follows this requirement it is acknowledged in OBD_FRF_ACK. Also the synchronization of OBD relevant ECUs is made by this signal:

Bit 3-5 is used for freeze frame acknowledgement.
Bit 2 is set, in case a driving cycle has started.
Bit 1 is set, in case a trip is finished.
Bit 0 is set, in case a warm up cycle is finished.

Bit 5, 4, 3 freeze frame status :
0 - No freeze frame stored
1 - Freeze frame requested by EMS
2 - Freeze frame requested by TCU
3 - Freeze frame requested by TCS
4~7 - Reserved";
BA_ "GenSigStartValue" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_ObdFrzFrmSta 0;
BA_ "UserSigValidity" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_ObdFrzFrmSta 3;
BA_ "NetworkRequestHoldingTime" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_ObdFrzFrmSta 0;
BA_ "RoutingFactor" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_ObdFrzFrmSta 5;
BA_ "Version" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_ObdFrzFrmSta "17.12.00";
BA_ "Description" SG_ 2214658049 ENG_EngClntTempVal "Engine coolant temperature in EMS sensed via an A/D converter; converted into degrees centigrade (°C).";
